      "summary": "Collection QC review: promoted to valid/ok; capture-interrupted status and the missing sixth dose row explained",
      "detail": "The device completed all six doses and parked itself; at 23:18 UTC (during dose 5's tap phase, right after nudge 10/10) the USB serial stream corrupted and the capture hung reading it, so the run document ends at dose 4 and carries status=capture-interrupted from the SIGINT recovery at 23:26:48 UTC, which flushed run.json and all CSVs intact. Dose 5 is reconstructed outside the doses array (run notes): the trace reaches 0.1701/0.2000 g at cycle 144, the bench camera at 23:28:57 UTC shows the run's final tare-relative mass static at 0.1635 g and the tube parked at 0 deg, and a 300 s post-run capture reads 164.9->164.5 mg; dose 5 therefore delivered ~0.1645 g, error ~-0.0355 g, stalled (nudge budget exhausted), ~560-900 s. Launch gate: held ~50 min while a -9.7 mg/min baseline drift decayed to a ~2 mg/min floor (zero shocks, jitter at display floor throughout); post-run diagnostic with MORE powder in the vessel reads -0.08 mg/min, attributing the drift to the vessel/enclosure drying, not the powder. Per-dose drift bias bounds: doses 0-2 (9-47 s) <2 mg; dose 3 (220 s) <7 mg; dose 4 (707 s) <20 mg, decaying through the run. The 50 mg triplet is complete and drift-immune; the recorded 200 mg pair is valid with the stated bounds.",
